# Performance and Optimization Rules

## Database — N+1 Problem

The most common performance trap. Do not make separate queries for each item when rendering lists.

```ts
// WRONG — N+1: separate author query for each thread
const threads = await db.thread.findMany()
for (const thread of threads) {
  thread.author = await db.user.findUnique({ where: { id: thread.authorId } })
}

// CORRECT — fetch with include in a single query
const threads = await db.thread.findMany({
  include: { author: { select: { username: true, avatarUrl: true } } }
})
```

## Database — Fetch Only What You Need

- Use `select` in `findMany()` or `findUnique()` calls
- Do not fetch large text fields (`content`) in list views; fetch them on detail pages
- Use `_count` to get related record counts without a separate query

```ts
// For listings — do not fetch content
const threads = await db.thread.findMany({
  select: {
    id: true, title: true, slug: true, createdAt: true,
    _count: { select: { posts: true } },
    author: { select: { username: true } }
  }
})
```

## Pagination

- Never fetch an entire list at once
- Offset-based: `skip` + `take` (for simple cases)
- Infinite scroll: cursor-based pagination (`cursor` + `take`)
- Default page size: 20 records

## Next.js Caching

- Server Component data fetches are automatically cached (Next.js 15 `fetch`)
- Add a cache layer for Prisma queries with `unstable_cache`
- Do not cache user-specific data (fetched with `cookies`, `headers`)
- Invalidate related pages with `revalidateTag`

```ts
import { unstable_cache } from "next/cache"

export const getCategories = unstable_cache(
  async () => db.category.findMany({ orderBy: { order: "asc" } }),
  ["categories"],
  { revalidate: 3600, tags: ["categories"] }
)
```

## React Suspense and Streaming

- Wrap slow data-fetching components with `<Suspense>`
- Define `loading.tsx` for every page
- Prepare skeleton components; do not return `null` or empty renders

```tsx
// page.tsx
export default function ThreadPage() {
  return (
    <>
      <ThreadHeader />
      <Suspense fallback={<PostListSkeleton />}>
        <PostList />
      </Suspense>
    </>
  )
}
```

## Image Optimization

- Use Next.js `<Image>` instead of `<img>`
- Always specify `width` and `height` props
- Set the `sizes` prop for small images like avatars
- Add a domain whitelist in `next.config.ts` for images from MinIO

## Bundle Size

- Load heavy libraries with dynamic imports
- Use `dynamic(() => import(...), { ssr: false })` for large components like editors
- Import only the used function, not the entire package

```ts
// Correct
import { format } from "date-fns"
// Wrong
import * as dateFns from "date-fns"
```

## Server Actions

- Server Actions do not open a new DB connection on each call (Prisma pooling)
- Combine parallelizable queries with `Promise.all`

```ts
const [threads, categories] = await Promise.all([
  getThreads(),
  getCategories(),
])
```

## Redis Cache

- Move frequently read, rarely changed data to Redis (category list, site settings)
- Use consistent naming for cache keys: `forum:categories`, `forum:user:{id}`
- Set TTLs based on content type (categories: 1 hour, thread list: 5 minutes)
